---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Barcelona Private Advisory"
  description="Barcelona-first private property advisory demo — curated shortlist, due diligence lens, negotiation support, and neighborhood-fit selection."
>
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">ABOUT</div>

    <h1 class="max-w-[760px] text-[30px] leading-[1.03] tracking-tight sm:text-[38px]">
      Private advisory,
      <br />
      not catalog.
    </h1>

    <p class="max-w-[760px] text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-black/58">
      This demo is not designed as a broad inventory portal. It presents a more selective product direction
      for Spain Costas: shortlist-first browsing, district-fit logic, due diligence signals, and calmer next-step support.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 space-y-10">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">PRODUCT DIRECTION</div>

        <h2 class="max-w-[620px] text-[28px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-[34px]">
          A premium real-estate experience shaped by selection, not by volume.
        </h2>

        <p class="max-w-[620px] text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-black/56">
          The advisory layer is the real differentiator: fewer options, clearer ranking logic,
          more visible trade-offs, and a stronger sense of neighborhood fit from the first screen.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-0 border-t border-black/10">
        {[
          ["Curated shortlist", "Inventory is ranked by fit, not by raw quantity. Lens + lifestyle logic sit above catalog browsing."],
          ["Due diligence lens", "Acquisition costs, restrictions, HOA signals, liquidity notes, and weak signals can be surfaced earlier."],
          ["Negotiation support", "The product can frame next-step logic, viewing support, offer strategy, and calmer buyer progression."],
          ["Barcelona Lens", "District-first browsing shifts the experience toward local fit: walkability, rhythm, noise, family logic, and daily texture."],
        ].map(([title, text]) => (
          <div class="grid gap-2 border-b border-black/10 py-4 last:border-b-0 sm:grid-cols-[180px_1fr]">
            <div class="text-[13px] font-medium">{title}</div>
            <div class="text-[12px] leading-[1.8] text-black/56">{text}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-0 border-y border-black/10 md:grid-cols-4">
      {[
        ["01", "Define", "Budget, districts, beds, lifestyle, and risk profile."],
        ["02", "Curate", "Rank by fit + lens. Shortlist first, not endless browsing."],
        ["03", "De-risk", "Surface fees, flags, restrictions, and negotiation prep."],
        ["04", "Close", "Support viewings, next steps, offer logic, and clarity."],
      ].map(([n, title, text]) => (
        <div class="border-b border-black/10 py-5 md:border-b-0 md:border-r md:px-5 md:last:border-r-0">
          <div class="text-[11px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/38">{n}</div>
          <div class="mt-3 text-[17px] tracking-tight">{title}</div>
          <div class="mt-2 max-w-[240px] text-[12px] leading-[1.75] text-black/56">{text}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-6 border-t border-black/10 pt-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.88fr_1.12fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">ADVISORY, NOT CATALOG</div>
        <div class="max-w-[460px] text-[28px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight">
          The value is not more listings.
          <br />
          The value is better calibration.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-[780px] text-[13px] leading-[1.9] text-black/56">
        This approach reduces decision fatigue and makes selection feel more premium.
        Instead of a wide, interchangeable catalog, the buyer sees a narrower, explainable shortlist
        shaped by district fit, acquisition profile, and next-step readiness.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 space-y-8">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-start">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">FAQ</div>

        <h2 class="max-w-[520px] text-[28px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-[34px]">
          Questions a client would actually ask.
        </h2>

        <p class="max-w-[520px] text-[13px] leading-[1.85] text-black/56">
          This section is intentionally written as client-facing reassurance, not product jargon.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-0 border-t border-black/10">
        {[
          ["Can clients update listings themselves?", "Yes — with a CMS layer such as Google Sheets, Airtable, or a CRM/feed adapter. The demo currently uses local data for speed and control."],
          ["Is this Barcelona-only?", "The product direction is intentionally Barcelona-first. Other geographies can be added later, but the premium advantage comes from local fit, not generic expansion."],
          ["What makes this premium?", "Controlled motion, editorial rhythm, shortlist + share, district logic, bilingual UX, and a calmer decision path rather than a loud portal experience."],
          ["What happens after the demo?", "Connect to live inventory or CRM, enable multilingual content editing, turn on analytics/SEO for production, and adapt the advisory tone to the final brand."],
        ].map(([q, a]) => (
          <div class="grid gap-2 border-b border-black/10 py-4 last:border-b-0 sm:grid-cols-[220px_1fr]">
            <div class="text-[13px] font-medium">{q}</div>
            <div class="text-[12px] leading-[1.8] text-black/56">{a}</div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-black/10 pt-8">
    <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-end">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="text-[12px] tracking-[0.18em] text-black/42">NEXT STEP</div>
        <div class="max-w-[620px] text-[24px] leading-[1.08] tracking-tight">
          Turn the demo into a real client-facing advisory site.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a
          href="/search"
          class="rounded-full border border-black/15 px-4 py-2 text-[12px] hover:border-black/25"
        >
          Start a search
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="rounded-full border border-black/10 px-4 py-2 text-[12px] text-black/70 hover:border-black/20 hover:text-black"
        >
          Contact
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
